On September 16, [Maine's First Ship](https://www.mfship.org/)'s reconstruction of the pinnace *Virginia* was heading up the Kennebec through Bath when her topmast made contact with the deck of the Carlton Bridge.
I happened to be photographing her at the time.

<%= f 'virginia-carlton-bridge.jpg', 'The wooden sailing vessel Virginia, with a red sail and an American flag flying, passing between the steel lift-span towers of the Carlton Bridge in Bath, Maine' %>

Nobody was hurt.
The ship's crew reported that safety protocols were followed throughout, and the Coast Guard is conducting the routine investigation that follows an incident like this.
Deck tours and daysails are paused while that runs its course.

